IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pa-individual`

-- Privacy Act 1988 (Cth), ss 6C, 6D, 6EA, 7B(3), APPs 7, 12, 13, Part IIIA (ss 6N, 6Q, 20K, 20R, 20T, 20W, 20X, 21C, 21D,
-- 21P), Part IIIC and Part V (ss 36, 40, 41) -- worked cases from the seat of the individual whose information is held.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, an OAIC determination, the Privacy Regulation 2013 or the CR code (neither was deposited).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_privacy-act-1988_baseline.py). Expected results
-- were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*): Chloe, 21, applies for a credit card and a credit
-- report is pulled (c043, 2024) and gets marketing calls and texts (c044, 2024). Jake, 24, takes two credit cards (k048,
-- 2031); owes $41,000 and collectors call (k064, 2037); his debt agreement completes on 31 May 2042 (k075). Daniel's company
-- Jarrah has three employees and "no Privacy Act yet" (d044, June 2031); in April 2036, above $3 million turnover, 1,200 users'
-- email addresses are breached (d052). The scenarios give no turnover figures, default dates, notice dates or the day the
-- debt agreement was MADE; the figures and dates used are the encoder's, chosen on the side of the line the scenario states.
-- Fixtures not named for an event are invented for the case.

