§ `Part IIIC -- data breaches (d052)`

#ASSERT `Is it an eligible data breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `1,200 users' email addresses taken, serious harm judged likely (d052)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it an eligible data breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `the same, serious harm judged not likely (d052)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it an eligible data breach` `Jarrah on 1 June 2031, first year, turnover assumed 400000 (d044)` `1,200 users' email addresses taken, serious harm judged likely (d052)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it an eligible data breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `an encrypted laptop lost, access not likely`)

#ASSERT (`Must I be told of the breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `1,200 users' email addresses taken, serious harm judged likely (d052)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `I must be told directly, as soon as practicable after the statement to the Commissioner is prepared`
#ASSERT (`Must I be told of the breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `1,200 users' email addresses taken, serious harm judged likely (d052)` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `not yet: the holder must first assess its suspicion, taking reasonable steps to finish within 30 days`
#ASSERT (`Must I be told of the breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `1,200 users' email addresses taken, serious harm judged likely (d052)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `I may be told directly, but need not be, because I am not at risk`
#ASSERT (`Must I be told of the breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `1,200 users' email addresses taken, serious harm judged likely (d052)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `I need not be told directly, because I am not at risk and only those at risk will be told`
#ASSERT (`Must I be told of the breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `1,200 users' email addresses taken, serious harm judged likely (d052)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the statement must be published on the holder's website and publicised`
#ASSERT (`Must I be told of the breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `1,200 users' email addresses taken, serious harm judged likely (d052)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `I need not be told, because remedial action means serious harm to me is not likely`
#ASSERT (`Must I be told of the breach` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `the same, serious harm judged not likely (d052)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `I need not be told, because it is not an eligible data breach`

#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner be given a statement` `Jarrah in April 2036, previous year turnover assumed 3400000 (d052)` `1,200 users' email addresses taken, serious harm judged likely (d052)` TRUE

§ `Part V -- complaints`

#ASSERT (`Will my complaint be investigated` `a Jarrah user's written complaint after complaining to Jarrah (d052)`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must investigate, subject to the other grounds in s 41`
#ASSERT (`Will my complaint be investigated` `the same, without first complaining to Jarrah (d052)`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must not investigate until I have complained to the respondent`
#ASSERT (`Will my complaint be investigated` `Jake's complaint that the bureau will not correct his file, made straight to the Commissioner (k064)`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must investigate, subject to the other grounds in s 41`
#ASSERT (`Will my complaint be investigated` `a complaint made 13 months after becoming aware`) EQUALS `the Commissioner must investigate, but may decline because I complained more than 12 months after I became aware`
#ASSERT (`Will my complaint be investigated` `a complaint by telephone`) EQUALS `not yet a complaint: it must be in writing and name the respondent`

